{
  "title": "Pipeline ingredient fixtures hold raw lines current extraction no longer produces",
  "description": "ramekin-core/tests/fixtures/ingredient_parsing/pipeline/ looks stale against current extraction. \
About 80 smittenkitchen fixtures still have blog lookback links as ingredients (\"1.5 Years Ago: Rhubarb Cream Cheese Handpies\", \"Six Months Ago: ...\"), which extract/blog.rs already filters out. \
For example, smittenkitchen--2014-12-jelly-doughnuts.json has them, but data/pipeline-snapshots/smittenkitchen-com_2014-12-jelly-doughnuts.json doesn't. make ingredient-catalog-audit reads these fixtures, so its pipeline-fixture numbers (Missing quantity, Unsupported quantity unit, unrecognized-name fingerprints) count junk lines that real imports never see. \
Other fixture lines may predate extractor fixes in the same way. \
Regenerate the pipeline fixtures from a fresh make pipeline run (make ingredient-tests-generate), review the fixture diff for raw-line changes, and commit it with the regenerated data/ingredient-catalog-audit.md. \
Found while checking p3-nutrition-amount-without-unit. \
Server/test-data only, so no web or iOS change.",
